\par\par \b \uc2 Kalshi\uc2 , to Combat Inside Betting, Plans Workplace Disclosure Rule --- Prediction market plans guardrails on some trades to curb suspicious activity\b0\par\par\uc2 By Brian Schwartz, Krystal Hur and Katherine Long \par \uc2 877 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 June 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  is planning to require that participants in some prediction markets disclose the identity of their employers, after an advisory committee recommended tighter security measures to combat potential insider trading and market manipulation.\par \par \uc2 Users seeking to make bets in some markets linked to material nonpublic information will be required to submit an online form disclosing where they work, \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  said. The changes are set to be rolled out in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 Sensitive betting markets related to issues such as company performance and national security, including the war in Iran, are expected to require employment disclosure, according to a \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  official.\par \par \uc2 In most cases, \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  won't verify the employment information provided by users unless the company learns of suspicious activity, a \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  spokeswoman said.\par \par \uc2 Once suspicious activity is flagged, the company will launch an investigation and seek proof of employment.\par \par \uc2 The increasing popularity of prediction markets such as \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  and \uc2 Polymarket\uc2  has compounded pressure on them to address suspicious activity, with lawmakers, regulators and prosecutors raising concerns about insider trading.\par \par \uc2 The changes being put in place by \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  come in response to a report from an audit committee, which recommended \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  collect employment information from users, according to a summary of the panel's findings.\par \par \uc2 Under \uc2 Kalshi\uc2 's current data collection system, "identifying potential insider relationships typically required manual review using publicly available information after trading activity had already occurred," the report says. Collecting employment information could improve "market surveillance analysis, early-stage investigative review, and deterrence."\par \par \uc2 The audit com]mittee is led by Brian Nelson, a former Treasury undersecretary for terrorism and financial intelligence; Daniel Taylor, the director of the \uc2 Wharton School\uc2 's forensic analytics lab; and \uc2 Lisa Pinheiro\uc2 , a managing principal at economic consulting firm \uc2 Analysis Group\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The company is also launching enhanced whistleblower features, \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The audit committee's report discloses for the first time that \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  has made more than 20 referrals to the \uc2 Commodity Futures Trading Commission\uc2  and the Justice Department during the first quarter of 2026.\par \par \uc2 Those who have been referred to federal authorities this year include former U.S. Rep. George Santos of New York and accounts linked to military spouses, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Accounts belonging to military spouses on \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  made accurate bets on when former President Nicolas Maduro of Venezuela would be ousted just days before he was seized by U.S. officials in January, according to a person familiar with the matter. At least one of those accounts was referred to federal investigators with the suspicion that a person using the spouse's account used nonpublic information to make that bet, the person said.\par \par \uc2 Kalshi\uc2 , which is regulated by the CFTC, enforces federal know-your-customer rules, known as KYC, mandating banks and brokers to require users to disclose their identities to prevent financial fraud and illicit activity.\par \par \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  requires users to give their address, at least part of their Social Security number, their phone number, date of birth and identity documentation. Users must be at least 18 years old.\par \par \uc2 In May, the exchange introduced new identity-verification measures including facial recognition in an effort to prevent minors from accessing their parents' accounts.\par \par \uc2 The prediction-market exchange has touted its use of KYC as a differentiator from its competitor, \uc2 Polymarket\uc2 , whose offshore platform doesn't require users to submit proof of identity.\par \par \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  recently backed the launch of Americans for Fair Markets, an advocacy group that supports "federally regulated, onshore exchanges vs. offshore platforms with no KYC and no recourse," according to the company.\par \par \uc2 In late February, \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  informed the CFTC and Justice Department about suspicions that \uc2 Santos\uc2  traded illegally in an event-based market that referenced his own appearance at this year's State of the Union address. \uc2 Santos\uc2  has denied any wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  said it uses a third-party vendor to block members of Congress, the president, cabinet secretaries, judges, other top government officials and their families from joining the platform. \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  also bans candidates running for public office, campaign employees and those working at polling stations from betting on election markets.\par \par \uc2 The changes come following two recent high-profile insider trading cases involving \uc2 Polymarket\uc2  users and a Congressional probe of how both \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  and \uc2 Polymarket\uc2  manage insider-trading risk.\par \par \uc2 In April, a U.S. soldier was charged with using classified information about the arrest of Maduro to trade on \uc2 Polymarket\uc2 . Last month, a \uc2 Google\uc2  employee was charged with using insider information about Google's annual search trends report to make $1.2 million on Polymarket.\par \par \uc2 In both cases, prosecutors at the Southern District of New York used information from other sources to bolster their identification of the defendants. Polymarket moved offshore and outside the strictures of U.S. regulations after a 2022 settlement with the CFTC.\par \par \uc2 Polymarket has touted its work with law enforcement in both cases. When the indictment against the Google employee was unsealed, the company's chief legal officer, Neal Kumar, posted on X, "Say it with me now -- it's not anonymous." Polymarket has a data partnership with Dow Jones, the publisher of The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260610em6a0000o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
