\par\par \b \uc2 Spotlight on Stocks\b0\par\par\uc2 505 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 June 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B9\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Broadcom\par \par \uc2 The semiconductor and software maker logged higher revenue in its latest quarter as demand for its AI chips accelerates. Still, shares tumbled 13% after it issued guidance that failed to live up to investor expectations.\par \par \uc2 Super Micro Computer\uc2 , \uc2 Advanced Micro Devices\uc2 , Intel\par \par \uc2 Shares of companies tied to AI fell after \uc2 Broadcom\uc2 's results prompted investors to take a breather on the highflying trade. Super Micro shares fell 1.1% in Thursday's trading, while AMD and Intel lost 3.6% and 0.9%, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Universal Music Group\par \par \uc2 Shares of the world's biggest music company slumped 4.9% after \uc2 Bill Ackman\uc2 's hedge-fund firm \uc2 Pershing Square\uc2  sold its stake valued at more than $1.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 Partners Group\par \par \uc2 The private-markets firm's shares regained some ground, adding 3.7% after tumbling Wednesday on news that it had capped redemptions at one of its funds. It said Thursday it expects a slowdown in growth in assets under management growth.\par \par \uc2 CrowdStrike\par \par \uc2 Shares slipped 3.8% on Thursday though the cybersecurity company yesterday raised its revenue guidance for the year.\par \par \uc2 Brown-Forman\par \par \uc2 The alcoholic-drinks company's shares rose 2.8% after it reported higher revenue in its fiscal fourth quarter.\par \par \uc2 Remy Cointreau\par \par \uc2 The maker of Remy Martin and Louis XIII cognac expects a return to sustainable organic sales growth and an improved margin in the year ahead. Shares rose 9.8% in France.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 FRIDAY'S EVENTS:\par \par \uc2 -- Economic data: Nonfarm payrolls data for May will be announced at 8:30 a.m. ET. The report will contain data on jobs added, the unemployment rate and hourly wages. Consumer credit data will also be released.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Shares of \uc2 Quantinuum\uc2  ended modestly higher Thursday after the quantum computing company raised $1.68 billion in an upsized IPO.\par \par \uc2 After opening around 1:30 p.m. ET, shares of the company rose 10% to about $66. The stock later pared those gains to end 0.6% higher at $60.38.\par \par \uc2 -- Heather Gillers\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Tech Sector Leads U.S. Layoff Plans\par \par \uc2 U.S.-based employers announced 97,006 job cuts in May with technology remaining the leading sector for staff reductions, according to a report from global outplacement and executive coaching firm \uc2 Challenger, Gray & Christmas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Employers in the tech sector announced 38,242 cuts last month. For the year, the tech sector has announced 123,653 cuts, up 66% through the same period in 2025.\par \par \uc2 Despite job cuts in the tech sector, overall layoffs have been largely stable. Job cuts this year were down 43% from the first five months of 2025, when reductions to the federal workforce drove totals to historic highs, the report said.\par \par \uc2 The survey found that AI was the leading reason for employers' job cuts for the third month in a row. For the year, AI has been cited in 22% of all layoffs.\par \par \uc2 "AI is now the leading reason companies give for cutting jobs and the primary industry citing it is technology," said \uc2 Andy Challenger\uc2 , chief revenue officer of \uc2 Challenger, Gray & Christmas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 -- Jessica Coacci\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw262\pich336\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3930\pichgoal5040
