\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: Deal Is Reached To End LIRR Strike\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alyssa Lukpat \par \uc2 333 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 May 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Unions representing \uc2 Long Island Rail Road\uc2  workers reached a deal with the \uc2 Metropolitan Transportation Authority\uc2  on Monday, the third day of a strike that halted the country's busiest commuter railroad.\par \par \uc2 New York Gov. \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  said phased train service would resume on Tuesday at noon.\par \par \uc2 She said the \uc2 MTA\uc2  and five unions representing the workers agreed to a "fair deal" on Monday night.\par \par \uc2 The governor, a Democrat, didn't disclose the terms of the deal but said the agreement "delivers raises for workers while protecting riders and taxpayers."\par \par \uc2 The strike was set to end at midnight, according to \uc2 Janno Lieber\uc2 , the head of the \uc2 MTA\uc2 , which oversees the \uc2 LIRR\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 MTA\uc2  is still advising riders to work from home on Tuesday if possible while train service is being fully restored.\par \par \uc2 About 3,500 \uc2 LIRR\uc2  employees walked off the job last weekend when their unions failed to reach a deal with the \uc2 MTA\uc2  after months of negotiations.\par \par \uc2 Roughly 300,000 daily passengers who travel between New York and Long Island were stranded. The \uc2 MTA\uc2  encouraged them to avoid nonessential travel. The agency offered limited shuttle bus service but warned it would be crowded.\par \par \uc2 LIRR\uc2  employees went on strike for the first time in three decades.\par \par \uc2 They wanted a wage increase of more than 4% for the next year of their contract to keep pace with inflation. The \uc2 MTA\uc2  offered a 3% raise.\par \par \uc2 The striking employees made over $135,000 on average in 2024, according to the \uc2 MTA\uc2 . They made closer to $200,000 factoring in health insurance and other benefits.\par \par \uc2 A coalition of five unions representing the workers returned to the bargaining table with the \uc2 MTA\uc2  on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Hochul said at a news briefing Monday night that the money to fund wage increases would "absolutely not" come from the state budget. "We stood firm for a deal that would not require any additional fare increases or tax increases," she said.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260519em5j0005v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
