\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: Rail Strike Threatens New York Commute\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alyssa Lukpat and Joseph Pisani \par \uc2 392 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 May 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Long Island Rail Road\uc2  strike carried into a second day Sunday, with weekday commutes looming and no sign of movement in the talks.\par \par \uc2 LIRR\uc2  employees walked off the job a day earlier over a wage dispute, shutting down the country's busiest commuter railroad. About 300,000 daily passengers will have to find alternative routes between New York City and Long Island.\par \par \uc2 Unionized railroad workers couldn't agree on a deal with the \uc2 Metropolitan Transportation Authority\uc2 , which oversees the LIRR, after months of negotiations.\par \par \uc2 LIRR\uc2  service has been halted during the railroad's first strike in three decades. The agency is offering limited shuttle-bus services toward Manhattan in the morning and to Long Island in the afternoon and evening, but it warned the buses would be slow-moving and crowded.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 MTA\uc2  planned to offer additional subway service in the city during the strike.\par \par \uc2 About 3,500 LIRR workers are on strike, represented by a coalition of five unions. The workers include locomotive engineers, machinists, electricians and signalmen.\par \par \uc2 The unions wanted a wage increase of more than 4% for the next year of their contract, starting in June. The \uc2 MTA\uc2  offered a 3% raise. In the past few years, \uc2 LIRR\uc2  employees received wage increases of 3% or 3.5%. The union said workers needed a 5% raise to keep up with inflation.\par \par \uc2 As contract negotiations dragged on, an emergency board appointed by President Trump said in March that the unions' requests were reasonable. New York Gov. \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , a Democrat seeking re-election in November, said Sunday the \uc2 MTA\uc2  had made multiple fair offers to the unions.\par \par \uc2 The unions and the \uc2 MTA\uc2  hadn't scheduled another round of talks, the coalition said Saturday. "We're far apart at this point," said Kevin Sexton, a vice president at the \uc2 Brotherhood of Locomotive Engineers and Trainmen\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 LIRR\uc2  workers last went on strike in 1994 largely over a pay dispute. After two days, former New York Gov. \uc2 Mario Cuomo\uc2 , a Democrat, forced \uc2 LIRR\uc2  management to settle with the unionized employees.\par \par \uc2 Hochul said the Trump administration cut mediation short, pushing talks toward a strike. Trump responded that he isn't to blame.\par \par \uc2 Hochul on Sunday called on the \uc2 MTA\uc2  and the unions to get back to the bargaining table.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260518em5i0000n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
