\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  Cuts 300 More Corporate Jobs --- Company will also close four regional offices as part of its effort to rebound\b0\par\par\uc2 By Heather Haddon \par \uc2 284 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 May 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B10\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  is laying off 300 U.S. workers and closing several regional corporate offices in the latest move by Chief Executive \uc2 Brian Niccol\uc2  to turn the coffee chain around.\par \par \uc2 The company said Friday that chain leaders had been told to find additional reductions beyond thousands of previous layoffs to streamline operations, lower costs and create a more sustainable business.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  said the 300 U.S. corporate roles are based in Seattle along with remote positions scattered around the country. They are in a variety of fields, including technology, marketing, finance, and research and development. Retail staff aren't affected.\par \par \uc2 The company said it is closing regional corporate offices in Chicago, Atlanta, Dallas and Burbank, Calif. It will maintain North American regional offices in New York, Toronto and Coral Gables, Fla., along with its Seattle headquarters and a new Nashville, Tenn., corporate hub. The $100 million office in Nashville is set to house 2,000 workers.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  is reviewing its international corporate offices for possible cuts. It is aiming to cut $2 billion in costs by the end of its 2028 fiscal year, helping balance out hundreds of millions of dollars in investment in cafe operations. The company is offering some executives stock bonuses valued at $6 million to reach the goals.\par \par \uc2 Last year \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  laid off roughly 2,000 corporate employees and eliminated hundreds of open positions. The chain closed hundreds of U.S. stores last year.\par \par \uc2 Layoffs across U.S. companies have exceeded 300,000 in the first four months of the year, according to outplacement firm \uc2 Challenger, Gray & Christmas\uc2 .\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw553\pich300\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal8295\pichgoal4500
