\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: Senators To Suspend Their Pay in Shutdowns\b0\par\par\uc2 By Terell Wright \par \uc2 288 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 May 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A5\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON -- Republican and Democratic senators unanimously adopted a resolution to suspend their pay during future government shutdowns, a measure designed to put more pressure on lawmakers to fund federal departments on time after record-setting lapses in the past year.\par \par \uc2 Sen. \uc2 John Kennedy\uc2  (R., La.) introduced the resolution, which passed the Senate on Thursday by a voice vote. The measure only applies to members of the Senate and doesn't need to be passed by the House or signed by President Trump. Lawmakers had drawn criticism in recent shutdowns for continuing to draw salaries while hundreds of thousands of federal employees were furloughed or working without pay.\par \par \uc2 The resolution stops the paychecks if Congress fails to provide funds for a federal agency or department. A senator wouldn't lose pay, as the money would be put in an escrow account until the shutdown ends. Funds would be withheld by the secretary of the Senate and released "as soon as practicable" when the funding lapse ends. Rank-and-file senators make $174,000 a year, and leaders earn $193,400.\par \par \uc2 The rule puts senators in the same boat as federal workers, who aren't paid when funding lapses. Employees typically are given back pay when funding is restored. During the recent funding lapse at the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 , the Trump administration shifted other money to pay airport-security workers and other employees.\par \par \uc2 The office of House Speaker Mike Johnson (R., La.) didn't respond to a request for comment on whether the House had similar plans.\par \par \uc2 (See related letter: "Letters to the Editor: Don't Let Aviation Workers Go Without Pay" -- WSJ May 21, 2026)\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260515em5f0000p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
