\par\par \b \uc2 Spotlight On Stocks\b0\par\par\uc2 838 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 May 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B10\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Cisco Systems\par \par \uc2 The tech conglomerate is cutting jobs so that it can pour more resources into silicon, optics, security and AI. Shares soared 13%.\par \par \uc2 Coinbase\par \par \uc2 The crypto exchange's stock rose 5.1% after a bill that would create a pathway for crypto to further upend traditional finance passed a key hurdle to becoming law. Other bitcoin-related stocks including \uc2 Robinhood\uc2  and Strategy also rose.\par \par \uc2 Cerebras Systems\par \par \uc2 The chip maker's shares soared more than 68% on their first trading day after the company raised $5.5 billion in the biggest IPO so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Doximity\par \par \uc2 The digital platform for U.S. healthcare professionals posted lower profit in the fiscal fourth quarter amid higher operating costs. Shares sank 23%.\par \par \uc2 Versant Media Group\par \par \uc2 The company's revenue and profit fell in its second quarter since being spun off from \uc2 Comcast\uc2 , but they were better than analysts expected. Shares rose 9.9%.\par \par \uc2 Klarna\par \par \uc2 Shares in the Swedish "buy-now, pay-later" company rallied 20% after it swung to a profit and gained market share.\par \par \uc2 Watches of Switzerland\par \par \uc2 The luxury-watch retailer expects revenue to rise over the next 12 months on strong demand, particularly in the U.S. Shares surged 19% in London.\par \par \uc2 Biogen\par \par \uc2 The biotech's shares fell 6.4% after the company's experimental drug for Alzheimer's disease failed to meet its main goal of showing that higher doses produced greater benefits for patients.\par \par \uc2 Burberry\par \par \uc2 The British trench-coat maker said sales jumped as it continues to undergo a turnaround plan, but shares fell 6.8% in London.\par \par \uc2 SMIC\par \par \uc2 China's biggest chip foundry reported weaker-than-expected net profit at the start of the year as it continued expanding capacity amid Beijing's push for chip localization. Shares of \uc2 Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corp.\uc2  fell 3.6%.\par \par \uc2 Applied Materials\par \par \uc2 The semiconductor-equipment maker gained more than 2% in after-hours trading after saying it expects stronger sales for its semiconductor business this year than it previously forecast.\par \par \uc2 Foxconn\par \par \uc2 Shares of the world's largest contract electronics maker fell 2.6% despite reporting robust first quarter revenue and profit as it ramped up production of server racks, other advanced equipment and consumer devices for the global artificial-intelligence build-out.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 FRIDAY'S EVENTS:\par \par \uc2 -- Empire State manufacturing survey for April.\par \par \uc2 -- The Fed will release data on industrial production and capacity utilization for April.\par \par \uc2 -- \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 's term as Fed chair comes to an end. He is due to be succeeded by Kevin Warsh, who passed key Senate votes this week.\par \par \uc2 EARNINGS EXPECTED:\par \par \uc2 Mizuho Financial\uc2 ,\par \par \uc2 Mitsubishi UFJ Financial\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Memory ETF\par \par \uc2 Sees Surge\par \par \uc2 A red-hot ETF that launched just six weeks ago has surpassed \uc2 Cathie Wood\uc2 's flagship ARK Innovation (ARKK) fund in assets.\par \par \uc2 Roundhill's Memory ETF, known by ticker DRAM, has accumulated some $9 billion in assets since its April 2 launch. The theme ETF tracks computer-memory and storage stocks, including companies like \uc2 Samsung\uc2  that don't trade in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Individual investors have been piling into the fund at an unprecedented pace for a new launch, according to data provider Vanda Research.\par \par \uc2 The ARK fund, which invests in high-growth tech companies, was once the poster-child for active thematic funds, though it bled assets after performance started to suffer. It became hugely popular with individual investors in the early 2020s and inspired other managers to launch hundreds of thematic ETFs trying to replicate its success.\par \par \uc2 None have caught on quite like the DRAM ETF.\par \par \uc2 -- Jack Pitcher\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Ruling Lifts\par \par \uc2 Truck Shares\par \par \uc2 Shares of trucking companies such as Old Dominion and J.B. Hunt rose after a Supreme Court ruling regarding broker liability raised expectations that there could be more business directed to the largest carriers.\par \par \uc2 The high court ruled that a man struck by a truck coordinated by C.H, Robinson, a freight brokerage, can sue the firm for negligent hiring. Brokerages match customers that need their goods transported to motor carriers.\par \par \uc2 Brokers face increased verification responsibilities and may direct customers to the larger trucking companies that have more resources for safety programs compared with smaller or newer carriers.\par \par \uc2 The decision also could gives the biggest players leeway to raise trucking rates. Shares of Old Dominion and J.B. Hunt and \uc2 Saia\uc2  gained 5.1%, 7.1% and 6.5% respectively.\par \par \uc2 -- Esther Fung\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Order Doubts\par \par \uc2 Hit \uc2 Boeing\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  shares dropped 4.7% after investors feared that China's long-awaited order of jets may be smaller than expected.\par \par \uc2 President Trump said Chinese leader Xi Jinping had agreed to order about 200 \uc2 Boeing\uc2  jets as part of a broader set of trade talks happening in Beijing this week, according to a clip from a Fox News interview posted Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  investors have been waiting for a flood of new orders from China for months. Beijing and Washington last year had been discussing a deal that could include fresh orders of hundreds of jets. Other media outlets had reported that as many as 500 jets could be part of the order.\par \par \uc2 -- Drew FitzGerald\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw262\pich246\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3930\pichgoal3690
