\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: \uc2 Walmart\uc2  to Cut, Relocate Workers\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sarah Nassauer \par \uc2 408 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 May 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Walmart\uc2  on Tuesday said it would cut or relocate about 1,000 corporate workers as it looks to combine more of its global-technology product teams, people familiar with the situation said.\par \par \uc2 This past summer, \uc2 Walmart\uc2  hired \uc2 Daniel Danker\uc2 , who was an \uc2 Instacart\uc2  executive, to fill a new role as head of global AI acceleration. Since then, Danker and \uc2 Walmart\uc2 's head of global technology, Suresh Kumar, have reviewed their internal structures and decided to streamline some teams to operate more efficiently, the leaders said in a memo sent to staff on Tuesday and viewed by The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 "In some cases, we've had different teams working on similar problems," they said in the memo. Affected staff can apply for open roles within the company, they said.\par \par \uc2 In recent years, \uc2 Walmart\uc2  has continually trimmed some corporate staff as it consolidates units and asks workers to relocate to its main corporate hubs. This year, \uc2 Walmart\uc2  planned 100 layoffs at its Hoboken, N.J., corporate offices, according to a layoff notice \uc2 Walmart\uc2  filed in New Jersey to comply with state law there.\par \par \uc2 This time around, many of the affected staff have been asked to relocate to \uc2 Walmart\uc2 's headquarters in Bentonville, Ark., or its Northern California offices, the people familiar with the situation said. \uc2 Walmart\uc2  is the country's largest private employer, with around 1.6 million U.S. employees.\par \par \uc2 Many large companies, including \uc2 Meta Platforms\uc2  and \uc2 Amazon.com\uc2 , have announced significant layoffs in recent months, often related to the need to invest heavily in artificial intelligence or planning for a time when more work is handled by AI. \uc2 Walmart\uc2 's changes are related to organizational structure and alignment, not handing over more tasks to AI, a \uc2 Walmart\uc2  spokeswoman said.\par \par \uc2 Walmart\uc2  has been on a sales-growth streak for years. Now it is investing heavily in technology, automation and AI efforts, while working to keep profits growing.\par \par \uc2 It has worked to expand its profits beyond the sales of goods through new businesses such as advertising and by reducing expenses, executives said during its earnings presentation this year.\par \par \uc2 This year, \uc2 Walmart\uc2  combined its global technology platforms across various units such as its warehouse chain, Sam's Club, \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and its international business.\par \par \uc2 "We believe this will result in our growth continuing to come at a much lower marginal cost than what it has historically," \uc2 Walmart\uc2  Chief Executive \uc2 John Furner\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260513em5d0000u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
