\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  to Cut 14% of Staff --- Crypto exchange said it would use more AI tools to speed up production\b0\par\par\uc2 By Joseph De Avila and Connor Hart \par \uc2 351 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 May 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  said it was laying off 700 employees as part of a restructuring effort to trim costs and streamline the cryptocurrency exchange's operations.\par \par \uc2 The restructuring would cut 14% of the company's workforce, \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  Chief Executive \uc2 Brian Armstrong\uc2  said Tuesday in a letter to employees.\par \par \uc2 The company said Tuesday it expects to record $50 million to $60 million in charges related to the cuts, primarily for severance and other employee termination costs. Most of those expenses are expected to hit in the second quarter.\par \par \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  said the move will help better manage operating expenses in the current market environment, as well as optimize operations for the artificial-intelligence era.\par \par \uc2 "AI is bringing a profound shift in how companies operate, and we're reshaping \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  to lead in this new era," Armstrong said. "This is a new way of working, and we need to leverage AI across every facet of our jobs."\par \par \uc2 The company employed 4,951 employees as of Dec. 31, according to the latest head count available in filings with the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The restructuring comes after bitcoin and major tokens have struggled to reclaim their 2025 highs, leaving \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 's business exposed to market swings. The job cuts mark the latest AI-related layoffs across the tech and crypto sectors.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, digital-currency exchange \uc2 Crypto.com\uc2  said it was trimming about 12% of its workforce, citing a push to integrate AI across the company.\par \par \uc2 In his letter Tuesday, Armstrong said AI is changing how the company works. Over the past year, \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  engineers have used AI to complete tasks in days that previously would take an entire team weeks of work, he said.\par \par \uc2 "The biggest risk now is not taking action," Armstrong said. "We are adjusting early and deliberately to rebuild \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  to be lean, fast and AI-native. We need to return to the speed and focus of our startup founding, with AI at our core."\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw262\pich444\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3930\pichgoal6660
