\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- Markets: \uc2 Cboe\uc2  Cuts Staff by 20%, Adds In-Office Workdays To Focus on Core Lines\b0\par\par\uc2 By Krystal Hur \par \uc2 485 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 May 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B10\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Cboe Global Markets\uc2  is slashing 20% of its global workforce and tightening its return-to-office policies, the newest plank in the exchange's plan to focus on key businesses.\par \par \uc2 About a fifth of \uc2 Cboe\uc2 's roughly 1,670 workers globally have been notified that they have been laid off, according to a memo Chief Executive \uc2 Craig Donohue\uc2  sent to employees Friday morning, which was seen by The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 The company is also offering a voluntary-retirement program to U.S. and Canadian workers who are at least 55 years old, have been with \uc2 Cboe\uc2  for at least five years.\par \par \uc2 The cuts are part of Donohue's strategy to allocate resources to its core, which includes index options, futures, foreign-exchange markets, and U.S. and European stocks.\par \par \uc2 Since his appointment as CEO in May 2025, he has taken steps to close \uc2 Cboe\uc2 's equities operation in Japan and sell the company's stock exchanges in Canada and Australia. Layoffs resulting from these changes are part of the 20% cut Donohue mentioned in his memo.\par \par \uc2 "I've been trying to reorient the company to be more focused on optimizing growth in our core," Donohue said in an interview, adding "This is allowing us to kind of pivot to these new areas of growth." Donohue said that \uc2 Cboe\uc2  intends to hire staff for its planned expansions into prediction markets, tokenization and clearing.\par \par \uc2 "We have a tremendous opportunity in front of us, but realizing it will require us to work more closely together and be incredibly disciplined with our decision-making, priorities, and allocation of capital," he wrote in the memo to employees.\par \par \uc2 "We will continue to aspire to be a high-performance, innovation-first, and ownership culture that can operate with the focus, accountability, and agility needed to execute our long-term growth strategy," he added.\par \par \uc2 Cboe\uc2  is also asking around 60% of its remote employees to relocate by an unspecified date to where they can commute to one of \uc2 Cboe\uc2 's offices in Chicago, New York, Kansas City, London, Amsterdam and Singapore. Employees will be offered a relocation package to help pay for costs, according to \uc2 Cboe\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some workers, including developers and those in IT, will still be allowed to work from home everyday.\par \par \uc2 Remote employees aren't eligible to be promoted into "people leadership roles," while some people already in such roles will continue to work remotely, since they "are tied directly to revenue generation and spend a significant amount of time outside of the office with clients already," Donohue wrote in his memo.\par \par \uc2 Starting July 6, employees will have to come in four days a week, up from the two days previously mandated.\par \par \uc2 Cboe\uc2 's stock is up 20% this year, and last month hit a record close of $309.38 per share.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260502em520005u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
