\par\par \b \uc2 Saks Global\uc2  Cuts 16% Of Corporate Staff As Part of Bankruptcy\b0\par\par\uc2 By Suzanne Kapner \par \uc2 266 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 May 2026\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Saks Global\uc2  is laying off about 16% of its corporate staff as it seeks to emerge from bankruptcy protection later this year, according to a person familiar with the situation.\par \par \uc2 About 640 jobs are being cut, representing less than 4% of the company's total workforce. The cuts don't include positions at retail stores or distribution centers, the person said. As of January, when \uc2 Saks\uc2  filed for bankruptcy protection, the company had about 17,000 employees.\par \par \uc2 Some of the cuts are a result of \uc2 Saks\uc2 's moves to exit businesses and streamline operations. Others are part of continuing changes resulting from its 2024 acquisition of \uc2 Neiman Marcus\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The strategic changes we are making to our corporate structure support the go-forward needs of the business, which will have a smaller operational footprint," said \uc2 Saks Global\uc2  Chief Executive \uc2 Geoffroy van Raemdonck\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Women's Wear Daily earlier reported the layoffs.\par \par \uc2 Since filing for bankruptcy, \uc2 Saks\uc2  has closed all but about 12 of its \uc2 Saks\uc2  Off Fifth discount stores.\par \par \uc2 It has slashed the number of \uc2 Saks Fifth Avenue\uc2  stores by almost half and closed several \uc2 Neiman Marcus\uc2  locations.\par \par \uc2 The company has been working to repair relationships with suppliers to ensure the flow of goods. The company said Thursday that its sales and inventory results were outperforming internal plans. That, along with capital commitments it has secured from investors, ensures the company will have enough liquidity to operate through the completion of its restructuring and pave the way for an emergence from court protection, the company said.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020260501em5100033\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
